# Client Intelligence Rule

When working on Nemo/SPRYTE customer workflows, treat `CLIENT.md` as part of the
database and prompt contract.

- Each paid `sites` row has a canonical `CLIENT.md` in
  `client_intelligence_files`.
- Before any agent/skill touches a customer account, load and pass the current
  `client_md` as the first business-context block.
- After meaningful actions, append a `client_intelligence_events` row and patch
  the canonical file.
- Weekly customer updates are `weekly_client_briefs`: two paragraphs max,
  plain English, grounded in `CLIENT.md` plus recent job evidence.
- Do not invent unknown business facts. Put them under **Open Questions**.
- Delivery is scored against **SEO/GEO Baseline (2026)** in CLIENT.md
  (Phases 1–4 from the home-services playbook). LVS insights update Phase 3.

Reference: `nemo-saas/docs/CLIENT_INTELLIGENCE.md`.
